  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Bapu Lal vs State on 6 July, 2017 Author: Chief Justice Bench: Chief Justice High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan At Jodhpur S.B. Criminal Revision No. 518 / 1996 Bapu Lal s/o Bheru Lal Gujar, resident of Gujaro Ka Fala Nakore, Police Station, Dhamotar, District Chittorgarh (At present Distt. Jail Pratapgarh) ----Petitioner Versus State of Rajasthan ----Respondent _____________________________________________________ For Petitioner(s) : Mr. Manish Sishodiya.",
    "facts": "2. Case of the prosecution is that Kunj Bihari Bhardwaj (PW-1), the Food Inspector, in presence of Kanak Mal Jain (PW-2), a shop owner and Mohan Singh (PW-3), an employee of the department purchased 'Khoya' (Mawa) from the petitioner. Sent to the public analyst for analysis, vide report Exhibit P-7 dated 19 th December, 1986, the sample was found to be adulterated inasmuch as milk fat content detected was 18%. As per the prescribed standard it had to be 20%. 3. The defence taken by the petitioner is that he was not in the business of sale of 'Khoya'. He had purchased the same for domestic consumption.",
